THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
===================

rashomon and pgraph, the two binaries the release archives and the plugin
archive carry, are both Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE). They are statically linked
and PURE GO -- CGO_ENABLED=0 -- so every third-party module is compiled INTO
the artifact you download, and its licence has to travel with it. This file
has a part for each binary: rashomon's first, then pgraph's.

No third-party module is linked into ./cmd/rashomon on any platform the
release ships. The binary is the Go standard library and this repository's
own packages. The one dependency it carried, a pure-Go SQLite driver and the
libc translation beneath it, read a proxy's store that no longer exists in
this project; both went with it.

This file is where the next dependency's notice is written before its code
ships. TestThirdPartyNotices_CoversEveryLinkedModule checks each part
against `go list -deps` of its own binary for every target the release
builds: rashomon's part against ./cmd/rashomon, pgraph's against
./cmd/pgraph in pgraph's own module under pgraph/. It fails if a module is
linked and not listed in its binary's part at its version, or listed there
and not linked, or, once any module is linked, if that part carries no
licence text at all. The check finds licence text anywhere in a part, not
beside each module, so each module's licence is written here by whoever
adds the module. TestThirdPartyNotices_CheckerFailsClosed runs the same
check against dependency lists of its own.

Modules linked into rashomon, in the order `go list` reports them:

  (none)

